  "details": "TLDR: Lower resolution in the peripherals, better performance, standard resolution in the center.\nFixed Foveated Rendering is a technique that lowers the rendering resolution on the edges of the VR display bordering and beyond what the lens allows the eyes to see. \nVRChat already has this rendering technique on the Quest. The already added VRSS can be configured to act identical to FFR by lowering the rendering resolution and shading rates on the edges to lower demand and increase frame-rate. It is only supported by Turing GPUs and is effectively VRSS but the shading-rate is reduced along the edges of the screen rather than increased.\nAlternatively, RDM, or Radial Density Masking is a technique to remove parts of the screen that are not visible, it would be effective as it supports all GPUs and not just Nvidia Turing GPUs, you can see the media here to see both of the techniques. \nhttp://media.steampowered.com/apps/valve/2016/Alex_Vlachos_Advanced_VR_Rendering_Performance_GDC2016.pdf",
